## How To Set Up Verification ##








## Host Commands [Note: Hosts can use all commands ] ##
/kick <user> #Kicks a user from the room (they can rejoin)
/ban <user> #Bans a user from the room for the whole session
/unban <user> #Unbans a user
/mute <user> #Stops a user from messaging
/unmute <user> #Unmutes a user
/lock #Locks the room from anyone else joining
/unlock #Unlocks the room so people can join
/advance #Shows advanced info about the room
/announce <msg> #Puts your message in huge font and highlighted 
/op <user> #Gives a user access to host commands
/unop <user> #Revokes host commands from a user

--Configs--
/config name <new_name> #Re-names the room
/config password <new_pw | none> #Changes the room password
/config domain <domain | none> #Changes the domains allowed in room
/config verify <on | off> #Changes the requirment of being verified in the room


## Non Host Commands ##
/quit #Leaves the room and puts you on the main screen
/who #Shows you who is in the room
/realname #Shows you the email address of each person and if they dont have one they are not verified
/msg <user> <msg> #Messages a user in the same room as you without anyone else able to see it
/server <msg> #Messages the host of the server
/share #Allows you to share a file to others in that room and let them download it through your device
/files #Shows you what files can be downloaded on the room
/download <id> #Downloads the file from the senders computer
/clear #Clears the current chat putting it back to how it would look when you join
/ui <1 or 2> #Lets you change the look of your messages in the room with 1 currently being the newest look and 2 being a more simple look


